{"id": "85929", "name": "סדרה הנדסית – איבר כללי מתוך איבר נתון ומנה (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Let term \\(n\\) of a geometric progression be denoted \\(u_{n}\\). Given that \\(u_{{CT:0}} = {{CT:1}}\\) and that the common ratio is \\(r={{CT:2}}\\) then</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\( u_{{CT:3}}= \\) [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Write both terms with the formula for the general term, then divide one by the other to eliminate the first term \\(a\\).</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The general term</b><br>Term \\(u_{n}\\) of a geometric progression with common ratio \\(r\\) and first term \\(a\\) is {{CT:4}}. So \\(u_{{CT:0}} = {{CT:5}} = {{CT:1}}\\) and \\(u_{{CT:3}} = {{CT:6}}\\).</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Eliminating \\(a\\)</b><br>Dividing \\(u_{{CT:3}}\\) by \\(u_{{CT:0}}\\) we eliminate \\(a\\) and obtain the equation<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ u_{{CT:3}} = {{CT:7}} \\]</p>Substituting \\(r={{CT:2}}\\) we find that<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ u_{{CT:3}}={{CT:8}} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "term_nval", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "SEQ-GEO-TRUE", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "SEQ-GEO-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "term_nval*rval", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "TERM_N_PLUS_ONE", "feedback": "<p>Your answer is term \\(u_{{CT:9}}\\) which is \\({{CT:1}}\\) multiplied by \\(\\left({{CT:2}}\\right)^{{{CT:3}} - {{CT:0}} + 1}\\). In fact \\(u_{{CT:3}}\\) is \\({{CT:1}}\\) multiplied by \\(\\left({{CT:2}}\\right)^{{{CT:3}} - {{CT:0}}}\\).</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "SEQ-GEO-FALSE-1", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "term_mval*rval^(mval-nval)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "M_MINUS_N", "feedback": "<p>Your answer is {{CT:10}} multiplied by \\(\\left({{CT:2}}\\right)^{{{CT:0}} - {{CT:3}}}\\). In fact \\(u_{{CT:3}}\\) is {{CT:10}} multiplied by \\(\\left({{CT:2}}\\right)^{{{CT:3}} - {{CT:0}}}\\).</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 3, "answernote": "SEQ-GEO-FALSE-2 ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 3, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "nval*rval", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "NR", "feedback": "<p>Your answer is {{CT:11}} multiplied by the common ratio {{CT:12}}. You may not be using the correct method.</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "SEQ-GEO-FALSE-3", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["amproduct", "anproduct", "aval", "mproductval", "mval", "mvalminus1", "n_minus_m", "n_minus_md", "np1", "nproductval", "nval", "nvalminus1", "r_magnitude", "r_sign", "rval", "term_mval", "term_nval", "un", "unr"], "nvariants": 50}